# dot_local/build-lan-repo/packages.list (chezmoi source)
#
# The AUR packages the lan-repo serves at http://raspberrypi:8080/ (the repo
# lives in $HOME/.local/arch-repo on the Pi and is rsynced from
# /home/jan/builds/repo/ on the build host). This is the policy file: after any
# run of the rebuild trigger, the repo serves exactly `packages.list` + latest
# versions — nothing more, nothing less.
#
# Each entry is an AUR package name. It publishes as `<name>-bin`, unless the
# entry already ends in `-bin`. The rebuild trigger on cyberkleiber (16:00
# daily) reconciles the repo against this list: packages that leave the list
# are dropped from the repo, everything left in it is built to its latest
# stable AUR version. No version pins — latest-stable at build time, every
# time.
hylki
rencal
